BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 736.0 Td (One-Sentence Summary) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 718.0 Td (This project is an interactive tool that helps football fitness coaches test a future) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 704.0 Td (  training plan and see whether each player's workload is likely to become too low,) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 690.0 Td (  normal, or risky over the next 15 days.) Tj ET
0.000 0.322 0.624 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 664.0 Td (1. The Main Sport-Science Idea) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 646.0 Td (The project focuses on ACWR, which means Acute:Chronic Workload Ratio.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 629.0 Td (- Acute workload: how much load the player has had recently, roughly the last 7 days.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 612.0 Td (- Chronic workload: the player's longer-term fitness/load base, roughly the last 28) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 598.0 Td (  days.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 581.0 Td (- ACWR: acute workload divided by chronic workload.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 564.0 Td (In simple terms: ACWR = recent workload / normal longer-term workload.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 547.0 Td (If a player suddenly has a very hard week compared with what he has been used to over) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 533.0 Td (  the last month, his ACWR rises.) Tj ET
0.000 0.322 0.624 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 507.0 Td (2. How To Interpret ACWR) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 489.0 Td (Undertraining: ACWR < 0.8. The player may not be receiving enough load stimulus.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 472.0 Td (Optimal: ACWR 0.8 to 1.3. The player is in a generally safe training range.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 455.0 Td (Caution: ACWR 1.3 to 1.5. The player may be approaching elevated workload risk.) Tj ET
0.933 0.196 0.306 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 438.0 Td (Danger: ACWR >= 1.5. The player may be overloaded and should be monitored closely.) Tj ET
0.933 0.196 0.306 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 421.0 Td (Important: this tool does not predict injuries directly. It predicts workload risk) Tj ET
0.933 0.196 0.306 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 407.0 Td (  signals. Coaches should combine it with medical information, wellness data, player) Tj ET
0.933 0.196 0.306 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 393.0 Td (  feedback, tactical needs, and staff judgment.) Tj ET
0.000 0.322 0.624 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 367.0 Td (3. What The Tool Does) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 349.0 Td (The tool lets coaches answer questions like: If we plan these sessions for the next 15) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 335.0 Td (  days, which players might enter a risky workload zone?) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 318.0 Td (The coach does not need to write code. They use a Streamlit app with two main parts:) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 301.0 Td (- Dashboard: shows the current ACWR status of the squad.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 284.0 Td (- Planning and Forecast: lets the coach create a 15-day plan and then forecasts future) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 270.0 Td (  ACWR.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 253.0 Td (Planned session types: G = game-based work / small-sided games; TAC = tactical; BP =) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 239.0 Td (  set pieces; TEC = technical; MATCH = official match; REST = no planned load.) Tj ET
0.000 0.322 0.624 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 213.0 Td (4. The Three Workload Metrics) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 195.0 Td (The project calculates ACWR separately for three football GPS/IMU metrics:) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 178.0 Td (- Total Distance: overall running volume. This reflects general aerobic and movement) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 164.0 Td (  load.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 147.0 Td (- Accelerations: high-intensity acceleration efforts. This reflects neuromuscular) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 133.0 Td (  stress.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 116.0 Td (- High-Speed Running: distance covered at high speed. This is important for sprint) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 102.0 Td (  exposure and high-speed running demands.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 85.0 Td (This matters because a player can look safe in total distance but risky in high-speed) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 71.0 Td (  running, or the opposite.) Tj ET
0.35 0.39 0.45 rg
