BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 736.0 Td (5. How The Project Works) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 718.0 Td (1. Historical player data is collected: past sessions, matches, player positions,) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 704.0 Td (  height, weight, age, and GPS workload metrics.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 687.0 Td (2. The data is cleaned and organized by day: the original drill-level data becomes one) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 673.0 Td (  row per player per day.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 656.0 Td (3. The project learns patterns from the past: for example, how much load a tactical) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 642.0 Td (  session usually creates for a player or position.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 625.0 Td (4. The coach enters a future plan: for example, tactical session tomorrow, match in) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 611.0 Td (  three days, recovery day after that.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 594.0 Td (5. The model predicts future daily loads for every player and every future day.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 577.0 Td (6. The app recalculates future ACWR by combining each player's real past workload with) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 563.0 Td (  the predicted future workload.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 546.0 Td (7. The app shows risk zones: optimal, undertraining, caution, or danger.) Tj ET
0.000 0.322 0.624 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 520.0 Td (6. Simple Analogy) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 502.0 Td (Think of each player like a car engine.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 485.0 Td (- The chronic workload is what the engine is used to handling.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 468.0 Td (- The acute workload is what we are asking it to do this week.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 451.0 Td (- If we suddenly ask too much compared with its normal level, the risk light turns on.) Tj ET
0.000 0.322 0.624 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 425.0 Td (7. Suggested Presentation Structure) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 407.0 Td (1. Problem: coaches need to plan training while avoiding sudden workload spikes.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 390.0 Td (2. Sport-Science Concept: explain acute workload, chronic workload, ACWR, and the risk) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 376.0 Td (  zones.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 359.0 Td (3. Data: football training and match data, player profile, position, session type, and) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 345.0 Td (  GPS load metrics.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 328.0 Td (4. Model: the project learns from previous sessions to estimate future load.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 311.0 Td (5. App: a coach creates a 15-day schedule, then the app forecasts ACWR and highlights) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 297.0 Td (  risk alerts.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 280.0 Td (6. Value: faster planning, player-specific monitoring, and clearer communication) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 266.0 Td (  between data staff and fitness coaches.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 249.0 Td (7. Limitations: no wellness or RPE data, ACWR is not a medical diagnosis, and results) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 235.0 Td (  depend on historical data quality.) Tj ET
0.000 0.322 0.624 rg
BT /F2 14 Tf 52.0 209.0 Td (8. One-Minute Presentation Script) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 191.0 Td (This project is a workload planning tool for football fitness coaches. It uses past GPS) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 177.0 Td (  training and match data to understand how different session types affect each player.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 163.0 Td (  The key metric is ACWR, which compares recent workload over about 7 days with longer-) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 149.0 Td (  term workload over about 28 days. If the recent load is too high compared with the) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 135.0 Td (  player's normal base, the player may enter a caution or danger zone.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 52.0 118.0 Td (In the app, a coach builds a 15-day training plan, and the system predicts how each) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 104.0 Td (  player's total distance, accelerations, and high-speed running will evolve. Then it) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 90.0 Td (  calculates future ACWR and highlights players who may be undertrained or overloaded.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 64.0 76.0 Td (  The goal is not to replace coaches, but to give them a clear decision-support tool) Tj ET
0.35 0.39 0.45 rg
BT /F1 8 Tf 277.5 30 Td (2) Tj ET
